# Brain Routing â€” Canonical Dispatch

## Single canonical router

```yaml
canonical_router:
  name:   ZeusRouter
  path:   "brain/runtime/src/lib.rs"
  status: WORKS (tests pass)
  
deleted_router:
  name:   BrainRouter
  path:   "brain/runtime/src/router.rs"
  status: DELETED (per CSA GAP-07 directive)
  was:    "string-switch on sio.runtime.provider â€” redundant, incorrect layer"
```

---

## ZeusRouter â€” dispatch logic

```yaml
entry_point: "ZeusRuntime::execute(ctx: ReasonCtx) -> Result<ReasonResult, BrainError>"

step_1_classify:
  fn:    "classify_complexity(action: &str, payload_size: usize) -> Complexity"
  path:  "brain/base/src/lib.rs"
  rules:
    Simple:  "payload_size < 256 AND action in [compute, route, validate, ping]"
    Medium:  "payload_size 256-2048"
    Complex: "payload_size > 2048"

step_2_select_ce:
  fn:    "ZeusRouter::select_ce(complexity) -> CeId"
  modes:
    AlgoOnly:  "all -> CeId::Algo"
    LocalLlm:  "Simple->Algo, Medium+Complex->Local"
    RemoteLlm: "Simple->Algo, Medium+Complex->Remote"
    Hybrid:    "Simple->Algo, Medium->Local, Complex->(Local if prefer_local else Remote)"

step_3_dispatch:
  CeId::Algo:   "AlgoParticle::reason(ctx)"
  CeId::Local:  "self.local_ce.as_ref()?.reason(ctx)  â€” None = graceful fallback to Algo"
  CeId::Remote: "self.remote_ce.as_ref()?.reason(ctx) â€” None = fallback chain Local->Algo"

hooks_called:
  before_route:    "hok://brain/before_route   (E4: pass-through)"
  after_route:     "hok://brain/after_route    (E4: pass-through)"
  before_execute:  "hok://brain/before_execute (E4: pass-through)"
  after_execute:   "hok://brain/after_execute  (E4: pass-through; E5: evidence pack)"
```

---

## ZeusConfig

```yaml
struct_ZeusConfig:
  mode:          "BrainMode â€” default Hybrid"
  max_local_ctx: "usize â€” default 4096 tokens; above this force Remote"
  prefer_local:  "bool  â€” default true; false for cloud-primary deployments"

e4_default: |
  ZeusConfig {
    mode:          BrainMode::Hybrid,
    max_local_ctx: 4096,
    prefer_local:  true,
  }
```

---

## CE injection pattern

```yaml
injection: |
  // E4 with CE.Algo only (default)
  let rt = ZeusRuntime::new(ZeusConfig::default());
  
  // After CE.Hacedle implemented (GAP-T5 resolved):
  let mut rt = ZeusRuntime::new(ZeusConfig::default());
  rt.router.register_local(Box::new(HacedleBrain::load("qwen.gguf")?));
  
  // E4.5 cloud:
  rt.router.register_remote(Box::new(RemoteBrain::new(racex_cfg)));

fallback_guarantee: |
  ZeusRouter never panics on missing CE.
  local_ce = None -> graceful fallback to AlgoParticle.
  remote_ce = None -> fallback to local, then Algo.
```

---

## BrainMode â€” SIO-level override

```yaml
mode_source: |
  BrainMode can be overridden per-request via RuntimeSio.runtime.mode field.
  Default comes from ZeusConfig::mode.

override_path: |
  RuntimeSio.runtime.mode -> InferRequest.mode_hint
    -> ZeusRuntime::execute_with_mode(ctx, mode_hint)
  
  Not yet implemented in InferenceEngine (GAP-T1).
  Wiring deferred until engine.rs receives InferRequest.
```

